 7. EXACT DATABASE SCHEMA DDL

The following SQL statements must be executed verbatim during the startup initialization block in Section 3.1. Execute each statement individually, in the exact order listed, wrapped in a try/except block that logs the statement and reraises on failure so the application refuses to start with a malformed schema.

sql
PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;
PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL;
PRAGMA synchronous = NORMAL;
PRAGMA busy_timeout = 5000;
PRAGMA cache_size = -64000;
PRAGMA temp_store = MEMORY;

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (
    id               INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    email            TEXT    NOT NULL UNIQUE COLLATE NOCASE,
    password_hash    TEXT    NOT NULL,
    display_name     TEXT    NOT NULL,
    role             TEXT    NOT NULL DEFAULT 'user'
                             CHECK(role IN ('user', 'admin')),
    is_active        INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1
                             CHECK(is_active IN (0, 1)),
    created_at       TEXT    NOT NULL,
    updated_at       TEXT    NOT NULL,
    last_login_at    TEXT
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS refresh_tokens (
    id           INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    user_id      INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    token_hash   TEXT    NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    expires_at   TEXT    NOT NULL,
    created_at   TEXT    NOT NULL,
    revoked      INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 CHECK(revoked IN (0, 1)),
    user_agent   TEXT,
    ip_address   TEXT
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS api_tokens (
    id           INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    user_id      INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    token_hash   TEXT    NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    label        TEXT    NOT NULL,
    created_at   TEXT    NOT NULL,
    last_used_at TEXT,
    revoked      INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 CHECK(revoked IN (0, 1))
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS transformations (
    id                  INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    user_id             INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    input_text          TEXT    NOT NULL,
    output_text         TEXT,
    model               TEXT    NOT NULL,
    status              TEXT    NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending'
                                CHECK(status IN ('pending','streaming','completed','failed')),
    error_message       TEXT,
    input_token_count   INTEGER,
    output_token_count  INTEGER,
    duration_ms         INTEGER,
    created_at          TEXT    NOT NULL,
    completed_at        TEXT
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS rate_limit_log (
    id            INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    user_id       INTEGER NOT NULL UNIQUE REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    window_start  TEXT    NOT NULL,
    request_count INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS app_config (
    key                 TEXT    PRIMARY KEY,
    value               TEXT    NOT NULL,
    updated_at          TEXT    NOT NULL,
    updated_by_user_id  INTEGER REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE SET NULL
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_users_email
    ON users(email);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_users_role
    ON users(role);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_refresh_tokens_user_id
    ON refresh_tokens(user_id);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_refresh_tokens_token_hash
    ON refresh_tokens(token_hash);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_refresh_tokens_expires_revoked
    ON refresh_tokens(expires_at, revoked);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_api_tokens_token_hash
    ON api_tokens(token_hash);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_api_tokens_user_id
    ON api_tokens(user_id);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_transformations_user_id
    ON transformations(user_id);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_transformations_status
    ON transformations(status);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_transformations_user_created
    ON transformations(user_id, created_at DESC);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_rate_limit_log_user_id
    ON rate_limit_log(user_id);


After executing all DDL statements, execute the following WAL checkpoint configuration check to verify WAL mode was successfully enabled:

sql
SELECT journal_mode FROM pragma_journal_mode();


If the returned value is not 'wal', log a critical warning: CRITICAL: WAL mode could not be enabled. Concurrent write performance will be degraded. Do not abort startup on this check — only log the warning.

Execute PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE) during the lifespan shutdown block (after the yield) to flush the WAL file before the process exits cleanly.



 8. COMPLETE BACKEND ROUTE CATALOG

Every route registered in main.py must appear in the following table. Implement them in this exact order within the file so that more specific routes are registered before catchall routes.

| Method | Path | Auth | Rate Limited | Description |
||||||
| GET | / | None | No | Serves index.html |
| POST | /api/auth/register | None | No | User registration |
| POST | /api/auth/login | None | No | Login, returns tokens |
| POST | /api/auth/refresh | None | No | Rotates refresh token |
| POST | /api/auth/logout | JWT | No | Revokes refresh token |
| DELETE | /api/auth/logout-all | JWT | No | Revokes all refresh tokens |
| GET | /api/users/me | JWT or API token | No | Get current user profile |
| PUT | /api/users/me | JWT or API token | No | Update profile / password |
| GET | /api/tokens | JWT or API token | No | List user's API tokens |
| POST | /api/tokens | JWT or API token | No | Create API token |
| DELETE | /api/tokens/{token_id} | JWT or API token | No | Revoke API token |
| POST | /api/transformations | JWT or API token | Yes | Create transformation job |
| GET | /api/transformations | JWT or API token | No | List transformations (paginated) |
| GET | /api/transformations/{id} | JWT or API token | No | Get single transformation |
| GET | /api/transformations/{id}/stream | JWT or token query param | No | SSE stream |
| DELETE | /api/transformations/{id} | JWT or API token | No | Delete transformation |
| GET | /api/admin/users | JWT (admin) | No | List all users |
| PUT | /api/admin/users/{user_id} | JWT (admin) | No | Modify user role/status |
| GET | /api/admin/stats | JWT (admin) | No | System statistics |
| GET | /api/admin/config | JWT (admin) | No | Read app config |
| PUT | /api/admin/config | JWT (admin) | No | Update app config |
| GET | /api/health | None | No | Health check (see Section 9) |
| GET | /{full_path:path} | None | No | SPA catchall, serves index.html |



 9. HEALTH CHECK ENDPOINT

Implement GET /api/health with no authentication requirement. This endpoint:

1. Opens a DB connection and executes SELECT 1 to verify the database is reachable.
2. Reads openai_api_key from app_config and checks if it is nonempty.
3. Returns 200 OK with the following body:
json
{
  "status": "healthy",
  "database": "ok",
  "ai_service_configured": true,
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "timestamp": "<current_utc_iso8601>"
}

4. If the database check fails, returns 503 with:
json
{
  "status": "unhealthy",
  "database": "error",
  "error": "<exception_message>",
  "ai_service_configured": false,
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "timestamp": "<current_utc_iso8601>"
}

5. The ai_service_configured field is true if openai_api_key is nonempty, false otherwise. This field is included in both the healthy and unhealthy response regardless of database status.



 10. SECURITY HARDENING REQUIREMENTS

The following security measures must all be applied within main.py and index.html. None of these are optional.

 10.1 HTTP Security Headers

Add a FastAPI middleware class that injects the following response headers on every response (including static file responses). Implement this as a custom BaseHTTPMiddleware subclass:


X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
X-Frame-Options: DENY
X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block
Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdn.tailwindcss.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdn.tailwindcss.com; font-src 'self' https://cdn.tailwindcss.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none';


For SSE endpoints (/api/transformations/{id}/stream), the CSP connectsrc must include 'self' to allow EventSource connections from the same origin.

 10.2 TimingSafe Token Comparison

All comparisons between submitted token hashes and stored token hashes must use hmac.compare_digest(stored_hash, submitted_hash) rather than the == operator, to prevent timing attacks. Apply this to refresh token lookups, API token lookups, and any other secret comparison operation.

 10.3 Password Hashing Parameters

The bcrypt cost factor is fixed at 12. Do not make this configurable. Log a startup message INFO: Password hashing using bcrypt rounds=12.

 10.4 JWT Secret Minimum Length

At module startup, after loading the JWT_SECRET environment variable, check that its length is at least 32 characters. If shorter, raise RuntimeError("JWT_SECRET must be at least 32 characters long.") to abort startup.

 10.5 Login BruteForce Protection

Implement a peremail failedlogin counter stored in a Python dict in memory (not in SQLite, since this is perprocess and ephemeral). Use a threading.Lock to make it threadsafe when accessed from async context via asyncio.get_event_loop().run_in_executor. The dict maps email_lowercase → {"count": int, "locked_until": datetime | None}. After 10 consecutive failed login attempts for a given email within a 15minute window, lock that email for 15 minutes. During lockout, the login endpoint must return 429 Too Many Requests with header Retry-After: <seconds_until_unlock> and body {"detail": "Too many failed login attempts. Try again in {N} minutes."}. A successful login resets the counter for that email.

 10.6 Sensitive Data Logging

The logger must never log: raw JWT values, raw refresh tokens, raw API tokens, passwords, the openai_api_key config value, or the Authorization header value. When logging request details, these fields must be redacted with [REDACTED].

 10.7 SQL Injection Prevention

All database queries must use parameterized statements (i.e., cursor.execute("SELECT ... WHERE id = ?", (user_id,))). String interpolation into SQL query text is forbidden in every location.

 10.8 Input Sanitization

All text fields stored in the database must be stored exactly as submitted (no HTML stripping or encoding at persistence time, since the frontend renders them as text not HTML). However, the frontend must never use .innerHTML or document.write() to display usersupplied content. All usersupplied text must be rendered via .textContent property assignment or within <pre> elements using .textContent. Any code path that needs to render dynamic HTML must construct DOM nodes programmatically (document.createElement, appendChild) with attribute values set via .setAttribute() or property assignment, never via string interpolation into innerHTML.



 11. DETAILED FRONTEND COMPONENT SPECIFICATIONS

 11.1 CSS Custom Properties and Theme

Within the <style> block, define the following CSS custom properties on :root:

css
:root {
  --color-bg-primary: #0f1117;
  --color-bg-secondary: #1a1d27;
  --color-bg-card: #1e2130;
  --color-bg-input: #252838;
  --color-border: #2e3347;
  --color-border-focus: #4f6ef7;
  --color-text-primary: #e2e8f0;
  --color-text-secondary: #8892b0;
  --color-text-muted: #4a5568;
  --color-accent-primary: #4f6ef7;
  --color-accent-hover: #6b84f8;
  --color-success: #48bb78;
  --color-warning: #ed8936;
  --color-danger: #fc5c5c;
  --color-danger-hover: #e53e3e;
  --color-streaming: #63b3ed;
  --font-mono: 'Fira Code', 'Cascadia Code', 'Consolas', 'Monaco', monospace;
  --radius-sm: 4px;
  --radius-md: 8px;
  --radius-lg: 12px;
  --shadow-card: 0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
  --transition-fast: 150ms ease;
  --transition-normal: 250ms ease;
}


The application uses a dark theme exclusively. All background colors, text colors, border colors, and input colors must use these CSS variables. Do not hardcode color values in Tailwind classes where a custom color is defined above — apply the custom properties via inline styles or custom CSS classes in the <style> block.

 11.2 Skeleton Loader Implementation

Define a CSS class .skeleton in the <style> block:

css
.skeleton {
  background: linear-gradient(
    90deg,
    var(--color-bg-card) 25%,
    var(--color-bg-input) 50%,
    var(--color-bg-card) 75%
  );
  background-size: 200% 100%;
  animation: skeleton-shimmer 1.5s infinite;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
}

@keyframes skeleton-shimmer {
  0%   { background-position: 200% 0; }
  100% { background-position: -200% 0; }
}


When constructing skeleton states for a view, define a function createSkeleton(width, height) in JavaScript that creates a <div> with class skeleton, sets its style width and height, and returns the element. Use the following skeleton dimensions for each view:

 Dashboard stat cards: two createSkeleton('100%', '80px') elements.
 Dashboard recent transformations: five createSkeleton('100%', '48px') elements separated by createSkeleton('100%', '1px') dividers.
 History table rows: ten createSkeleton('100%', '40px') elements.
 Transformation detail — input block: createSkeleton('100%', '120px').
 Transformation detail — output block: createSkeleton('100%', '400px').
 Admin stats grid: eight createSkeleton('100%', '100px') elements.
 Admin users table: eight createSkeleton('100%', '44px') elements.

 11.3 Toast Notification System

Define a JavaScript class ToastManager with:
 A static MAX_VISIBLE_TOASTS = 5 constant.
 An internal array activeToasts tracking currently visible toast elements.
 A method show(message, type, duration = 4000):
  1. Creates a <div> with role="status" and aria-live="polite".
  2. Sets its textContent to message.
  3. Applies color classes: success = background: var(--color-success), error = background: var(--color-danger), info = background: var(--color-accent-primary).
  4. Common styles: position: fixed, bottom: 1.5rem, right position calculated based on activeToasts.length * 0, stacked vertically from bottom.
  5. Applies a CSS transition: opacity 200ms ease, transform 200ms ease. Initial state: opacity: 0; transform: translateY(10px). After appending to DOM, sets opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0) in a requestAnimationFrame callback.
  6. If activeToasts.length >= MAX_VISIBLE_TOASTS, removes the oldest toast immediately before adding the new one.
  7. After duration ms, fades out (sets opacity to 0, translateY back to 10px), then removes from DOM after transition ends.
  8. Clicking the toast dismisses it immediately.
 A method success(message) that calls show(message, 'success').
 A method error(message) that calls show(message, 'error').
 A method info(message) that calls show(message, 'info').

Instantiate const toast = new ToastManager() at module level. All toast calls in the application use this instance.

 11.4 Confirmation Modal

Define a reusable JavaScript function showConfirmModal({ title, message, confirmText, confirmClass, onConfirm }). This function:

1. Creates a fullscreen overlay <div> with role="dialog", aria-modal="true", aria-labelledby="modal-title", positioned fixed, background rgba(0,0,0,0.7), z-index: 9999, centered flex.
2. Inside the overlay, creates a modal card <div> with maxwidth 28rem, padding, background var(--color-bg-card), borderradius var(--radius-lg), boxshadow var(--shadow-card).
3. The card contains:
    An <h2 id="modal-title"> with title.
    A <p> with message.
    A flex row with "Cancel" button (grey) and confirm button (class confirmClass, text confirmText).
4. "Cancel" click: remove overlay from DOM.
5. Confirm click: call onConfirm(), then remove overlay from DOM.
6. Pressing Escape triggers the cancel behavior.
7. Clicking outside the modal card (on the overlay itself) triggers the cancel behavior.
8. On open, move focus to the confirm button. On close, move focus back to the element that was focused before the modal opened.
9. Append the overlay to document.body. Return a cleanup function that removes it.

 11.5 Router Implementation

Define a JavaScript class Router with:
 A routes Map that stores pattern → { render: AsyncFunction, requiresAuth: boolean, requiresAdmin: boolean }.
 A method register(pattern, handler, options).
 A method navigate(hash) that sets window.location.hash = hash.
 A method handleRoute() that:
  1. Reads window.location.hash or defaults to #/.
  2. Strips the # prefix.
  3. Iterates registered routes to find a match. Routes with path parameters (e.g., /transformation/:id) use a simple regex where :param is replaced with ([^/]+) and the match groups are extracted.
  4. If no match, renders the 404 view.
  5. If the route has requiresAuth: true and AppState.user is null, stores the current hash in sessionStorage.setItem('pendingRedirect', window.location.hash) and calls navigate('#/login').
  6. If the route has requiresAdmin: true and AppState.user.role !== 'admin', renders the 403 view.
  7. Otherwise, calls render(params) on the matched route handler and awaits it.
  8. Scrolls window to top: window.scrollTo(0, 0).
 A method init() that calls addEventListener('hashchange', () => this.handleRoute()) and addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => this.handleRoute()).

Register all routes in the Router at the bottom of the <script> block, before calling router.init(). All route render functions must be async and must clear and replace the contents of document.getElementById('app-root').

 11.6 Streaming Output Panel — Full Behavioral Specification

The output <pre id="output-pre"> element must have the following CSS applied:

css
#output-pre {
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 0.875rem;
  line-height: 1.7;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
  word-break: break-word;
  overflow-y: auto;
  max-height: 70vh;
  min-height: 200px;
  background: var(--color-bg-input);
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  padding: 1rem;
  color: var(--color-text-primary);
}


Track a boolean userHasScrolledUp = false. Attach a scroll event listener to #output-pre. In the handler, if pre.scrollHeight - pre.scrollTop - pre.clientHeight > 50, set userHasScrolledUp = true. If the user scrolls back to within 20px of the bottom, set userHasScrolledUp = false. In the streaming chunk handler, only autoscroll if !userHasScrolledUp:

javascript
if (!userHasScrolledUp) {
  pre.scrollTop = pre.scrollHeight;
}


Display a "↓ Jump to bottom" pill button in the bottomright corner of the output panel when userHasScrolledUp is true and streaming is active. Clicking it sets userHasScrolledUp = false and scrolls to bottom.

Track a tokenCount = 0 variable. For each received chunk, increment it by the number of characters divided by 4 (rough token approximation). Display a live ~{tokenCount} tokens counter below the output area, updating every 10 chunks to avoid excessive DOM writes.

 11.7 New Transformation View — Resume Mode

When #/new is loaded and window.location.hash contains the substring ?resume=, extract the transformation ID. On render, call GET /api/transformations/{id}. If the transformation is completed, populate #output-pre with output_text and show the action buttons. If it is failed, show the error banner. If it is pending or streaming, start the SSE connection immediately as if the user had just submitted a new transformation — do not rerender the input panel for resume mode. For resume mode, the input textarea must be populated with the transformation's input_text (readonly, since the job is already created), and the model selector must show the job's model (also readonly/disabled).

 11.8 Keyboard Shortcuts

Implement the following keyboard shortcuts via document.addEventListener('keydown', ...):

 Ctrl+Enter (or Cmd+Enter on Mac, detected via event.metaKey || event.ctrlKey): If the current route is #/new and the Generate button is enabled (not disabled), trigger the Generate button click handler.
 Escape: If a modal is currently open, close it (same as clicking Cancel/X on the modal).
 Ctrl+Shift+N (or Cmd+Shift+N): Navigate to #/new.
 Ctrl+Shift+H (or Cmd+Shift+H): Navigate to #/history.

Prevent default browser behavior for all matched shortcuts with event.preventDefault().



 12. COMPLETE ERROR HANDLING AND ERROR MESSAGE CATALOG

Every possible error state in the application has an explicit uservisible message. The following catalog is exhaustive. Any error not listed here must display a fallback message: "An unexpected error occurred. Please refresh the page and try again."

 12.1 Registration Errors

| Condition | Field | Message |
||||
| Display name empty after trim | display_name | "Display name is required." |
| Display name < 2 chars | display_name | "Display name must be at least 2 characters." |
| Display name > 80 chars | display_name | "Display name must not exceed 80 characters." |
| Email empty | email | "Email address is required." |
| Email invalid format | email | "Please enter a valid email address." |
| Password empty | password | "Password is required." |
| Password < 10 chars | password | "Password must be at least 10 characters long." |
| Password missing uppercase | password | "Password must contain at least one uppercase letter." |
| Password missing lowercase | password | "Password must contain at least one lowercase letter." |
| Password missing digit | password | "Password must contain at least one number." |
| Password missing special char | password | "Password must contain at least one special character (!@$%^&()_+=[]{}|;:,.<>?)." |
| Confirm password mismatch | confirm_password | "Passwords do not match." |
| Server: email taken (409) | email | "An account with this email address already exists." |
| Network error | form (top) | "Registration failed. Please check your internet connection." |

 12.2 Login Errors

| Condition | Display Location | Message |
||||
| Email or password wrong (401) | Below password field | "Invalid email or password." |
| Account locked due to bruteforce (429) | Below password field | "Too many failed attempts. Try again in {N} minutes." |
| Network error | Toast (error) | "Login failed. Please check your internet connection." |
| Server error 5xx | Toast (error) | "A server error occurred. Please try again later." |

 12.3 Transformation Errors

| Condition | Display Location | Message |
||||
| Input too short | Below textarea | "Description must be at least {min} characters. Currently {n} characters." |
| Input too long | Below textarea | "Description must not exceed {max} characters. Currently {n} characters." |
| Rate limit exceeded (429) | Toast (error) | "Rate limit reached. You can run {limit} transformations per hour. Try again in {N} minutes." |
| AI service not configured (503) | Output panel error banner | "The AI service is not currently configured. Please contact your administrator." |
| OpenAI authentication error | Output panel error banner | "AI service authentication failed. The API key may be invalid. Please contact your administrator." |
| OpenAI rate limit (from OpenAI) | Output panel error banner | "The AI service is temporarily ratelimited. Please wait a moment and try again." |
| OpenAI context length exceeded | Output panel error banner | "The input is too long for the selected model. Please shorten your description." |
| Network error during stream | Output panel error banner | "Connection lost during generation. The partial result has been saved. You can view it in your history." |
| EventSource error event | Output panel error banner | "Streaming connection failed. Please try again." |

 12.4 General Errors

| Condition | Display Location | Message |
||||
| Accessing protected route without auth | Redirect to #/login | (no message; after redirect, pending route is restored) |
| Accessing admin route as nonadmin | Inline in #app-root | "403 — Forbidden. You do not have permission to access this page." |
| GET /api/transformations/{id} returns 404 | Inline in #app-root | "Transformation not found. It may have been deleted." |
| Token refresh fails on 401 | Toast (error) + redirect | "Your session has expired. Please log in again." |
| Deleting streaming transformation (409) | Toast (error) | "This transformation is currently running and cannot be deleted." |
| API token create limit reached (400) | Toast (error) | "You have reached the maximum of 10 active API tokens. Please revoke an existing token before creating a new one." |
| Profile update with wrong current password (400) | Below current password field | "Current password is incorrect." |
| Admin: trying to deactivate self | Toast (error) | "You cannot deactivate your own account." |
| Admin: trying to demote self | Toast (error) | "You cannot remove admin privileges from your own account." |



 13. PAGINATION COMPONENT

Define a reusable JavaScript function createPagination({ currentPage, totalPages, onPageChange }) that returns a DOM element. The element contains:

 A "Previous" <button> with aria-label="Previous page". Disabled when currentPage === 1.
 A text node " Page {currentPage} of {totalPages} ".
 A "Next" <button> with aria-label="Next page". Disabled when currentPage === totalPages or totalPages === 0.
 A "Go to page" <input type="number"> with min="1", max="{totalPages}", value="{currentPage}", aria-label="Go to page number", visible only when totalPages > 5. When the user changes the value and presses Enter or blurs the field, clamp the value to [1, totalPages] and call onPageChange(clampedValue).

Previous/Next button clicks call onPageChange(currentPage - 1) and onPageChange(currentPage + 1) respectively. The function returns the container element. When totalPages <= 1, return null (no pagination needed). Callers check for null before appending.



 14. DATE AND TIME FORMATTING

Define a JavaScript utility object DateUtil with the following methods:

 formatDateTime(isoString) → returns a string in the format "MMM DD, YYYY HH:MM UTC", e.g. "Feb 22, 2026 11:48 UTC". Uses new Date(isoString) and Date.prototype methods. Always displays in UTC.
 formatRelative(isoString) → returns a humanreadable relative time string: "just now" (< 60s), "2 minutes ago" (< 60m), "3 hours ago" (< 24h), "2 days ago" (< 7d), then falls back to formatDateTime. Uses Date.now() as reference.
 formatDuration(ms) → if ms is null/undefined, returns "—". If ms < 1000, returns "{ms}ms". If ms < 60000, returns "{(ms/1000).toFixed(1)}s". Otherwise returns "{Math.floor(ms/60000)}m {Math.round((ms%60000)/1000)}s".
 formatNumber(n) → if null/undefined, returns "—". Otherwise formats with toLocaleString('en-US') for thousands separators.

Use these methods consistently across all views. Never inline date formatting logic outside of this utility object.



 15. DOCKER AND DEPLOYMENT CONFIGURATION

The following files must be created alongside main.py and index.html as part of the deliverable.

 15.1 Dockerfile

dockerfile
FROM python:3.12-slim

WORKDIR /app

RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
    curl \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

COPY requirements.txt .
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt

COPY main.py .
COPY index.html .

RUN groupadd -r appuser && useradd -r -g appuser appuser
RUN mkdir -p /data && chown appuser:appuser /data

USER appuser

ENV DATABASE_PATH=/data/app.db
ENV FRONTEND_PATH=/app/index.html
ENV LOG_LEVEL=INFO

EXPOSE 8000

HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=10s --start-period=15s --retries=3 \
  CMD curl -f http://localhost:8000/api/health || exit 1

CMD ["uvicorn", "main:app", "--host", "0.0.0.0", "--port", "8000", "--proxy-headers", "--forwarded-allow-ips", "*"]


 15.2 dockercompose.yml

yaml
version: '3.9'

services:
  app:
    build: .
    container_name: prompt-transformer
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "8000:8000"
    volumes:
      - app_data:/data
    environment:
      - JWT_SECRET=${JWT_SECRET}
      - ADMIN_EMAIL=${ADMIN_EMAIL}
      - ADMIN_PASSWORD=${ADMIN_PASSWORD}
      - ALLOWED_ORIGINS=${ALLOWED_ORIGINS}
      - DATABASE_PATH=/data/app.db
      - FRONTEND_PATH=/app/index.html
      - LOG_LEVEL=${LOG_LEVEL:-INFO}
    env_file:
      - .env
    healthcheck:
